WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.290
August might seem like a slow month for movies,
but that doesn't mean there isn't plenty of

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.290
entertainment available.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.540
One of the best ways to wind down the summer
is by watching trailers for what's ahead—glimpses

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.370
of the horror, romance, action, and drama
that's set to arrive in theaters over the

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.220
coming months.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.580
Here are all the August trailers that are
guaranteed to blow you away.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.000
mother!

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.900
Written and directed by Darren Aronofsky,
mother!

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.050
Stars Jennifer Lawrence and Javier Bardem
as a couple whose peaceful existence is disturbed

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:30.030
when guests show up in their home—a simple
premise that, as the trailer suggests, may

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.800
not actually be so simple.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.240
The trailer offers a thrilling and terrifying
glimpse at Aronofsky's newest attempt to mess

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.440
with our heads, featuring creepy imagery along
with deeper hints at the film's disturbing

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:40.940
plot.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.460
Sign us up for whatever nightmares mother!
has to offer.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.400
The Wilde Wedding

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.430
Basically the main you need to know about
The Wilde Wedding is that Patrick Stewart

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.580
has hair, but the rest of it looks pretty
good, too.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.020
Stewart plays Harold, a writer preparing to
marry retired film star Eve, played by Glenn

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:56.520
Close.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.140
The guests at their wedding include John Malkovich
as Eve's ex-husband, as well as Minnie Driver,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.520
Grace Van Patten, Orange is the New Black's
Yael Stone, and The Americans' Noah Emmerich.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.320
Killing Gunther

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.110
Arnold Schwarzenegger is the most feared hitman
in the business in the upcoming action comedy

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.260
Killing Gunther, written and directed by Saturday
Night Live veteran Taran Killam.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:20.440
Schwarzenegger stars as Gunther, who becomes
the target of an assassination plot from his

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.200
fellow hitmen.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.280
Killam's directorial debut seems both stylish
and funny, and Schwarzenegger, while only

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.800
appearing briefly in the trailer, looks great
in his role as a ridiculously skilled assassin.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.260
"Go ahead, kill me!"

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.280
Mark Felt: The Man Who Brought Down the White
House

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:40.060
Liam Neeson plays Deep Throat in the true
story of Mark Felt, an FBI agent became the

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.300
Watergate whistleblower for Washington Post
reporters Bob Woodward and Carl Bernstein.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.850
The talented cast is rounded out by Diane
Lane, Tony Goldwyn, Josh Lucas, and Michael

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:49.420
C. Hall.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.380
Literally, Right Before Aaron

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.340
Justin Long stars in Literally, Right Before
Aaron as Adam, a man still reeling from his

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.080
recent break-up when his ex-girlfriend calls
him to let him know she's getting married.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.260
Adam agrees to go to the wedding, and predictably,
things quickly take a turn for the worse.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.120
The Florida Project

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.840
Sean Baker's Tangerine follow-up The Florida
Project has all the heart and beauty shown

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.300
in his earlier work, albeit in a new setting.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:17.940
This time, Baker investigates the lives of
those living in an extended-stay motel in

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:22.450
Orlando, focusing specifically on a precocious
six-year-old and the motel's owner Bobby,

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.460
played by Willem Dafoe.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.060
Dafoe is the grounding force of the trailer,
but the child actors are given the chance

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:27.960
to shine as well.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.720
Already enjoying rave reviews, The Florida
Project looks like a beautiful, touching exploration

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.460
of childhood.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.580
Brawl in Cell Block 99

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.140
It's Vince Vaughn like you've never seen him
before in the trailer for Brawl in Cell Block

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:44.000
99, the latest action outing from Bone Tomahawk
director S. Craig Zahler.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.380
Vaughn plays Bradley Thomas, a former boxer
who resorts to drug running in an effort to

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.190
save his marriage after losing his job as
a mechanic.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.520
Things quickly go wrong when a drug deal turns
deadly, putting him behind bars.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.440
Goodbye Christopher Robin

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.010
The new trailer for Goodbye Christopher Robin
stars Domhnall Gleeson as A.A.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.960
Milne, the author who dreamed up Winnie the
Pooh for his young son Christopher Robin.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.180
Margot Robbie takes on the part of Milne's
wife Daphne in the film.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:13.070
The trailer deals heavily with Milne's struggle
with PTSD, but manages to balance drama, humor,

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:17.340
and heart in a way that will hopefully translate
into an affecting biopic.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.130
Batman vs. Two-Face

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.880
Adam West's final performance as Batman is
teased in the trailer for Batman vs. Two-Face.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.910
The Batman legend reprised his role alongside
Burt Ward's Robin, with the two facing off

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.960
against Harvey Dent, voiced by William Shatner,
in this sequel to 2016's Batman: Return of

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.990
the Caped Crusaders.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.800
Suburbicon

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.100
Directed by George Clooney from a script co-written
by the Coen brothers, Suburbicon stars Matt

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.500
Damon as Gardner Lodge, a man dealing with
the violent advances of a loan shark in his

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.770
small, 1950s-era American town.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:52.120
Oscar Isaac and Julianne Moore costar, and
with so many huge names attached, it looks

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:56.240
like Suburbicon is a town audiences won't
want to leave—even if the residents most

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.040
definitely do.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.870
Last Flag Flying

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:03.459
Break out the tissues before you watch the
trailer for Richard Linklater's Last Flag

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:04.459
Flying.

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:08.600
Steve Carell leads the dramedy as Richard
"Doc" Shepherd, who recruits two of his Vietnam

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.510
buddies, played by Bryan Cranston and Laurence
Fishburne, to help him bury his son after

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.830
he's killed in Iraq.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.190
The three leads have great chemistry, and
their growing bond helps anchor what looks

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.209
like an emotional cross-country journey.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:21.540
Death Wish

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:25.570
Bruce Willis is out for vigilante justice
in the first trailer for Eli Roth's Death

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.120
Wish, a remake of the 1974 film of the same
name.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.370
The movie follows Willis as Paul Kersey, a
doctor who seeks revenge after the violence

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.220
in the streets of Chicago spills into his
own home.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:39.720
While remakes are old hat at this point, Death
Wish looks like it could be worth a trip to

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.510
the theater.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:42.710
Molly's Game

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:47.490
Jessica Chastain stars as the smart, straight-talking
Molly Bloom in the first trailer for Aaron

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.880
Sorkin's directorial debut Molly's Game, which
tells the true story of the Olympic-class

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:55.120
skier who ran an exclusive high-stakes poker
game.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.210
As the trailer shows, the movie follows Molly
on her way up in the poker world while also

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.520
showing her downfall.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.300
Chastain also has some impressive backup in
the movie, with costars Idris Elba [IH-dris,

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.190
not "eye-dris"] and Michael Cera.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.460
Call Me By Your Name

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:12.610
This film festival darling stars Armie Hammer
as Oliver, an American professor who travels

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:15.370
to northern Italy in the summer of 1983.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:19.060
While there, he falls into a relationship
with a 17-year-old Italian boy.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:23.070
With an early 100 percent on Rotten Tomatoes,
Call Me By Your Name clearly isn't a movie

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.750
you want to miss.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.570
Super Troopers 2

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.710
It's been a long, long time coming, but the
first trailer for the upcoming Super Troopers

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.630
2 is finally here…and it's awesome.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.640
The sequel to the cult cop comedy features
the group of Vermont state troopers fighting

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.389
with Canada over the borderline, setting up
a new Highway Patrol station right in the

00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:41.560
conflicted zone.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.700
Considering the fact that the original writers,
directors, and cast are all on board, this

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.890
sequel should be well worth the wait.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.460
"Not so funny meow, is it?"

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:51.850
Gemini

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.699
Explore the dark side of celebrity in the
trailer for Gemini.

00:05:54.699 --> 00:05:58.960
The movie stars Lola Kirke as Jill, an assistant
to a Hollywood starlet named Heather, played

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.260
by Zoë Kravitz.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:04.150
When Heather is murdered, Jill learns she's
a suspect, causing her to reevaluate her own

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.530
views of friendship, truth, and fame.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.930
The trailer hints that there could be more
to Heather's murder than meets the eye, raising

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.330
a whole bunch of questions to be answered
in the film.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.590
With already stellar reviews from its film
festival premieres, Gemini is a stylish murder

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.310
mystery we're looking forward to figuring
out.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.919
The Death of Stalin

00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:25.389
Veep creator Armando Iannucci is about to
satirize yet another country's government,

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:27.850
judging by the first trailer for The Death
of Stalin.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:31.960
The movie shows the mad rush for power after
Stalin's passing, with Jeffrey Tambor, Steve

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.960
Buscemi, and Jason Isaacs playing characters
looking to take charge.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.760
"When I said no problem what I meant was:
No.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:39.760
Problem."

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:44.229
It may not be a Game of Thrones-level fight
for power, but we're definitely on board to

00:06:44.229 --> 00:06:46.180
watch this not-so-historical comedy.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.180
Thanks for watching!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.440
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.760
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

